BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Dennis RedMoon Darkeem
DTSTART:20261112T230000Z
DTEND:20261113T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:41c07a8292f2a1b934beb8edeb4813f5644e9e93@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Dennis RedMoon Darkeem\nNovember
  12\, 2026 6:00 pm⁠–⁠7:00 pm\nStudio Theater\nJoin us in The Studio 
 Theater for Dennis RedMoon Darkeem's Artist-in-Residence lecture. Darkeem 
 is a Bronx-based interdisciplinary artist and educator whose work explores
  cultural identity\, environmental transformation\, and community engageme
 nt through mixed media\, sculpture\, photography\, and installation. His p
 ractice often draws on Afro-Indigenous diasporic traditions to create work
  rooted in storytelling\, sustainability\, and social awareness.\nDuring t
 his residency\, Darkeem will focus on creating innovative solutions using 
 waste and unused glass materials. His goal is to engage youth through work
 shops that transform recycled glass\, photography\, and lighting into expe
 rimental\, dimensional artworks.\nReservations for this event are not requ
 ired. This lecture is free and open to the public.\nArtist presentations r
 eflect the individual artist's perspective\, practice\, and personal views
 \, and do not represent an official position of the Corning Museum of Glas
 s.\nPresentations may occasionally touch on personal\, sensitive\, or diff
 icult subject matter.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9
 b0uzpj/event/78514536/20261112180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78514536/20261112180000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Hoseok Youn
DTSTART:20261112T230000Z
DTEND:20261113T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:4b638073d420bde63a88892093b69988dad64b2a@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Hoseok Youn\nNovember 12\, 2026 
 6:00 pm⁠–⁠7:00 pm\nStudio Theater\nJoin us in The Studio Theater for
  Hoseok Youn's Artist-in-Residence lecture. Youn is a South Korean glassbl
 ower specializing in the demanding tradition of Venetian-style glassworkin
 g\, known for its thin-walled vessels\, precise bit work\, and assemblies 
 requiring exact timing. Drawing inspiration from pop culture\, science fic
 tion\, fantasy\, and the games and toys of his childhood\, Youn fuses thes
 e influences into distinctive glass figures constructed from cups\, vessel
 s\, and stemware\, employing a wide decorative vocabulary.\nDuring his 202
 6 residency at The Studio\, Youn plans to expand his current series by dev
 eloping reliable methods to encode special patterns and images into the gl
 ass body using two complementary techniques: terra cotta mold blowing and 
 wheel engraving.\nReservations for this event are not required. This lectu
 re is free and open to the public.\nArtist presentations reflect the indiv
 idual artist's perspective\, practice\, and personal views\, and do not re
 present an official position of the Corning Museum of Glass.\nPresentation
 s may occasionally touch on personal\, sensitive\, or difficult subject ma
 tter.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/785
 14538/20261112180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78514538/20261112180000
END:VEVENT
