SUMMARY:Urban Sketchers Corning at the National Soaring Museum
DTSTART:20261114T180000Z
DTEND:20261114T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:86a9d6ae5bcdfa8d92ad9cb83695b752bd550b5c@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art,Community,Connection,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:The National Soaring Museum (NSM)\, perched atop Harris Hill j
 ust outside Elmira\, New York\, stands as one of the only two museums in t
 he United States dedicated exclusively to the preservation and celebration
  of motorless flight.\nHarris Hill and Elmira are widely regarded as the 
 “Soaring Capital of America\,” thanks to more than 80 years of rich so
 aring history — a heritage that continues to draw aviators\, historians
 \, and enthusiasts from around the world.\nCapture the history of soaring 
 with us at the National Soaring Museum on Harris Hill! Meet inside the ent
 rance at 1:00 pm on Saturday\, Nov 14. We'll sketch\, then meet for a sket
 chbook throwdown at 2:45.\nBring your sketching supplies\, your sketchy fr
 iends\, and a folding stool or chair if you like to sit to sketch. Remembe
 r\, it's a museum\, so open water containers are not allowed\, but water b
 rushes are fine.\nHappy Sketching!\nWhere: National Soaring Museum\, 51 So
 aring Hill Drive\, Elmira\, NY\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.t
 ime.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515461/20261114130000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515461/20261114130000
END:VEVENT
