BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A History of the Old Stone Heap
DTSTART:20261117T000000Z
DTEND:20261117T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:5d3d1dbfafa1f2e6c915bc7b66f16537eb3f9434@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:Event by The History Center in Tompkins County\n110 North Tiog
 a Street within the Tompkins Center for History & Culture\, Ithaca\, NY\nD
 uration: 1 hr\nPublic\nAuthor Jean Cochrane will tell stories from her res
 earch about The Old Stone Heap\, the oldest standing home in Ithaca.\nThe 
 many lives of this home\, also known as Davenport’s Tavern\, have engage
 d a full arc of community life across more than two centuries. From the Ga
 yogo̱hó꞉nǫʔ to pioneer settlers on a farm that wrapped around the Ca
 yuga Inlet to West Hill\; from village presidents to professors\; from ten
 ant farmers to an Arts and Crafts acolyte\; from the Voice of Cornell Foot
 ball to a grumpy old man whose deathbed testament left the Heap in limbo f
 or years. Images of this New World Dutch stone house will illustrate its a
 rchitectural uniqueness and multiple transformations across time\, includi
 ng rare scenes from a Wharton Brothers silent film. Sparked by curiosity a
 bout Cochrane’s ancestors’ interlude here as dairy farmers\, her resea
 rch weaves together social and architectural history to reveal a home with
  “one of the finest views in Tompkins County.”\nThis presentation will
  include a powerpoint and Q&A\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.ti
 me.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515560/20261116190000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515560/20261116190000
END:VEVENT
