BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Muses and Makers: Flute and Lyre
DTSTART:20261120T173000Z
DTEND:20261120T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:1f515e72c4c85ee7815f6dd3450af41bb74ff9cd@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art,History & Heritage,Music
DESCRIPTION:Muses and Makers:\nFlute and Lyre\nFriday\, Nov 20\, 2026\n12:
 30-2PM / Robinson Lecture Hall\, Floor 2L\nFocusing on Greek mythology thr
 ough figures such as Eurydice\, Syrinx\, Hermes\, Orpheus\, Pan\, and othe
 rs\, this program explores the age-old Apollonian and Dionysian duality em
 bodied by the lyre and the flute.\nThrough music by Kuhlau\, Mouquet\, Deb
 ussy\, and Beethoven\, alongside works of art from the Museum’s collecti
 on\, the presentation traces the fascinating\, sometimes violent mythologi
 cal origins of these instruments\, their symbolic significance\, and the w
 ays in which they shape the fates of those who encounter them. Across cent
 uries\, these stories invite reflection on love\, loss\, transformation\, 
 and the relationship between humans and the divine.\nPresenters will inclu
 de Athena Kirk\, Associate Professor of Classics\; Patricia Garcia Gíl\, 
 Postdoctoral Associate and Artist-in-Residence\, Cornell Center for Histor
 ical Keyboards\; Roger Moseley\, Associate Professor of Music and Director
 \, Cornell Center for Historical Keyboards\; Wendy Rolfe\, Professor of Fl
 ute\, Berklee College of Music\; and the Museum’s Andrew C. Weislogel\, 
 the Seymour R. Askin\, Jr. ’47 Curator\, Earlier European and American A
 rt.\nCosponsored by the Cornell Center for Historical Keyboards.\n\nSource
 : FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515474/202611201
 23000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515474/20261120123000
END:VEVENT
