CATEGORIES:History & Heritage,Education
DESCRIPTION:Event by The History Center in Tompkins County\n110 North Tiog
 a Street within the Tompkins Center for History & Culture\, Ithaca\, NY\nD
 uration: 2 hr\nPublic\nSince 1976\, INHS has strengthened neighborhoods an
 d changed lives by combining community leadership\, housing opportunity\, 
 education\, and investment to help people build stability\, equity\, and b
 elonging. Come explore our history at the History Center in Tompkins Count
 y\, where we are pleased to present INHS: Homes\, Hope\, and Opportunity S
 ince 1976\, an exhibit on INHS’s roots and impact\, on display in the at
 rium from Nov. 21 through February.\nPlease join us for an opening recepti
 on on Saturday\, Nov. 21\, from 1–3 pm at the History Center to kick off
  the exhibit and celebrate our 50 years of bringing safe\, stable\, afford
 able housing to the residents of Ithaca\, Tompkins County\, and beyond. Re
 ception will include an overview of INHS history\, impact\, and the people
  and partnerships that helped shape the organization.\nReception - 1:00 PM
 -3:00 PM\nPresentation from Kate G. de la Garza\, INHS Executive Director 
 - 1:30 PM-2:15 PM\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uz
 pj/event/78515558/20261121130000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515558/20261121130000
