BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Snowy Day at the Clemens Center
DTSTART:20261121T190000Z
DTEND:20261122T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:5477f8393b00c1fd2cb1ec55b99615bb8b06cf6d@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Family Fun
DESCRIPTION:Community Foundation of Elmira-Corning and the Finger Lakes Fa
 mily Connex Series presents\nTHE SNOWY DAY AND OTHER STORIES\nSaturday\, N
 ovember 21\, 2026 @2:00pm\nOpen to all\nGeneral Admission Tickets:\n$15 Ad
 ult\; $7.50 Youth Under 18\nFacility maintenance fees apply.\nLimited to 5
 00 seats\nFor tickets and more information\, call or visit the Clemens Cen
 ter Box Office at 607-734-8191 or 800-724-0159 Monday-Friday 11:30am to 5:
 30pm\, or visit ClemensCenter.org.\n---------------\nThe Snowy Day celebra
 tes the magic and boundless possibilities of the first snowfall! Follow Pe
 ter and his friends as they romp and play\, starting snow ball fights and 
 making snow angels in this imaginative musical play about the childhood jo
 ys and challenges of growing up. Using innovative shadow puppetry\, Keats
 ’ treasured characters come to life in this humorous and fun adaptation 
 of Whistle for Willie\, Goggles!\, A Letter to Amy\, and The Snowy Day.\nT
 his is a 50-minute Sensory-Friendly performance specifically designed to s
 erve children and adults on the autism spectrum or any sensory or social c
 ognitive disorders.\nAdjustments to the production include:\n– house lig
 hts dimmed (but not off)\n– no strobes or flashing lights\n– consisten
 t sound volume\n– explanation of what will be seen and heard – narrato
 rs in the story\n– quiet area in the venue (Mandeville Hall)\n– fidget
 s welcome\n– audience encouraged to talk and react\n– ability to leave
  your seats\n– If you need to use a specific electronic device\, such as
  an iPad\, to help with your enjoyment of the show\, please inform the ush
 ers as you enter the theatre.\n– sensory-friendly activities are availab
 le in the second floor lobby\, for use before or during the performance\nA
 ge Recommendation: All Ages\nAll children 12 months and older need a ticke
 t\nDates/times/programs/prices are subject to change.\n---------------\nCo
 mmunity Foundation of Elmira-Corning and the Finger Lakes 2026-27 Family C
 onnex Series\nThe carefully-curated programs in the Family Connex Series w
 ill help connect families to the Clemens Center by attending together\, an
 d promote family conversation\, critical thinking\, and the simple enjoyme
 nt of the live performing arts.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.
 time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507406/20261121140000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507406/20261121140000
END:VEVENT
