 pm\, or visit ClemensCenter.org.\n---------------\nThe Snowy Day celebrate
 s the magic and boundless possibilities of the first snowfall! Follow Pete
 r and his friends as they romp and play\, starting snow ball fights and ma
 king snow angels in this imaginative musical play about the childhood joys
  and challenges of growing up. Using innovative shadow puppetry\, Keats’
  treasured characters come to life in this humorous and fun adaptation of 
 Whistle for Willie\, Goggles!\, A Letter to Amy\, and The Snowy Day.\nThis
  is a 50-minute Sensory-Friendly performance specifically designed to serv
 e children and adults on the autism spectrum or any sensory or social cogn
 itive disorders.\nAdjustments to the production include:\n– house lights
  dimmed (but not off)\n– no strobes or flashing lights\n– consistent s
 ound volume\n– explanation of what will be seen and heard – narrators 
 in the story\n– quiet area in the venue (Mandeville Hall)\n– fidgets w
 elcome\n– audience encouraged to talk and react\n– ability to leave yo
 ur seats\n– If you need to use a specific electronic device\, such as an
  iPad\, to help with your enjoyment of the show\, please inform the ushers
  as you enter the theatre.\n– sensory-friendly activities are available 
 in the second floor lobby\, for use before or during the performance\nAge 
 Recommendation: All Ages\nAll children 12 months and older need a ticket\n
 Dates/times/programs/prices are subject to change.\n---------------\nCommu
 nity Foundation of Elmira-Corning and the Finger Lakes 2026-27 Family Conn
 ex Series\nThe carefully-curated programs in the Family Connex Series will
  help connect families to the Clemens Center by attending together\, and p
 romote family conversation\, critical thinking\, and the simple enjoyment 
 of the live performing arts.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.tim
 e.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78508376/20261121140000
GEO:42.08921;-76.804956
LOCATION:Clemens Center\, 207 Clemens Center Parkway\, Elmira\, New York\,
  14901
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78508376/20261121140000
END:VEVENT
