BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wear Vibrant Colors 2: Dare To Dance Album Advance
DTSTART:20261121T233000Z
DTEND:20261122T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:4172ab7843c6b3e44be6f17aa3dd7eaea7ab48d4@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Food
DESCRIPTION:Event by Papa Muse\, Maddy Walsh Artist Page and 3 others\nThe
  Nocturnal Café\nDuration: 5 hr\nPublic\nOn November 21st\, Papa Muse wil
 l host the second annual Wear Vibrant Colors show at the Nocturnal Cafe in
  downtown Ithaca.\nGet Advanced Discounted Tickets and ensure a spot.\nOnl
 ine at www.PapaMuse.com or at The Nocturnal Cafe until day of show.\nNew P
 apa Muse Album:\nListen to the first song on the upcoming album "Faith We 
 Are Growing" at: https://papamuse.com/music\nABOUT the Party:\nThis perfor
 mance will be the Dare to Dance Album Advance\, a full-length album that P
 apa Muse began working on 7 years ago. And while the album will not be ava
 ilable to the public until January 15th\, attendees of Wear Vibrant Colors
  2 will get early access to the album.\nPotluck Dinner:\nLike last year\, 
 there will once again be a scrumptious potluck dinner that starts at 6:30 
 p.m.\, followed by a plethora of talented musical acts starting at 7:00 p.
 m. Feel free to bring a dish to share (plates and utensils will be provide
 d)\, but do not bring drinks\, as the Nocturnal Cafe will provide an elabo
 rate selection.\nCome wearing vibrant colors and be part of our live music
  video shoot! There will also be viewing areas and comfortable seating for
  those camera-shy\, bashful folks.\nPerformers:\nPapa Muse:\nWith a deep-r
 ooted history in the Ithaca music scene—as former producer of Musefest\,
  the Band and Breakfast\, and other innovative endeavors—Papa Muse has s
 pent the last decade fervently devoted to his musical craft. The songwrite
 r continually presents a compelling live performance\, and on this special
  night\, he will perform with his full band and even a few guests. They wi
 ll play tracks from the upcoming Dare to Dance album\, along with a few ne
 wer tunes.\nPublic Water Supply:\nHailing from Rochester\, Public Water Su
 pply is a powerhouse 4-piece outfit blending danceable and cosmic outlaw c
 ountry with high-octane psychedelic indie rock. Driven by soaring and uniq
 uely distinctive lead vocals\, dazzling guitar work\, and an irresistible 
 groove\, their electrifying live show delivers an unforgettable\, genre-be
 nding punch.\nMadd Daddy:\nFeaturing powerhouse vocalist Maddy Walsh (of M
 addy Walsh & The Blind Spots) alongside her father\, Ted Walsh\, this belo
 ved Ithaca father-daughter duo will join the party with a set filled with 
 unexpected covers\, "blood harmonies\," and finger-picked acoustic guitar.
  Expect seamless chemistry\, charm\, and maybe a rare original woven into 
 the mix.\nMax Moses / Lady Loveday\nLady Loveday & Max Moses will share th
 e stage\, swapping songs starting at 7:00 p.m. Each has something unique t
 o offer:\nLady Loveday:\nLoveday Greene brings her signature "swoon countr
 y" to the stage\, blending theatrical vocal power with raw\, cinematic sto
 rytelling. With a background spanning opera\, rock\, and country\, her int
 oxicating voice creates an atmosphere that is equal parts tender and twang
 y.\nMax Moses:\nKnown as a driving force behind Ithaca favorite Cast Iron 
 Cowboys\, Max Moses joins us for a solo set blending soulful country blues
 \, fingerstyle guitar\, and heartfelt songwriting and storytelling.\nTicke
 ts: $10 in advance or $15 at the door. $5 Discount with Student ID. Get ad
 vance tickets at the Nocturnal Cafe or online at PapaMuse.com. Reserve you
 r spot today.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/e
 vent/78514642/20261121183000
GEO:42.43916;-76.500519
LOCATION:The Nocturnal Cafe\, 103 South Geneva Street\, Ithaca\, New York
 \, 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78514642/20261121183000
END:VEVENT
