DESCRIPTION:Event by Watkins Glen Public Library\n214 N Franklin St\, Watk
 ins Glen\, NY 14891-1224\, United States\nDuration: 1 hr 30 min\nPublic\nD
 r. Gary Emerson is back with a new Reading & Discussion Series! This is a 
 graduate-level discussion comprised of eight ( total sessions. All books a
 re provided by the Watkins Glen Public Library for the duration of the pro
 gram.\nParticipants are asked to attend as many sessions as possible.\nReg
 istration is required due to limited space and copies of materials. To reg
 ister\, call (607) 535-2346\, or visit us in person.\nAll programs run fro
 m 6:00pm-7:30pm and will be hosted in the Watkins Glen Area Chamber of Com
 merce Conference Room (214 N Franklin Street\, Watkins Glen\, NY). Space i
 s limited.\nAUGUST 4 - With Malice Toward None\nAUGUST 25 - Battle Cry of 
 Freedom\nSEPTEMBER 8 - Battle Cry of Freedom\nSEPTEMEBER 29 - This Republi
 c is Suffering\nOCTOBER 20 - Daughters of the Union\nNOVEMBER 10 - Embattl
 ed Freedom\nNOVEMBER 24 - Marching Home\nDECEMBER 8 - Reconstruction: A Co
 ncise History\nThis project is made possible in part by funds from the Sta
 tewide Community Regrant Program\, a regrant program of the New York State
  Council on the Arts with support from the Office of the Governor and the 
 New York State Legislature\, and administered by the Arts Council of the S
 outhern Finger Lakes.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9
 b0uzpj/event/78440615/20260825180000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78440615/20260825180000
