BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening Day: World's Largest Traveling Harmonica Museum at Marich 
 Music\, Corning
DTSTART:20261128T170000Z
DTEND:20261128T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:2618991b7d402fda071d07eeb13b42c902277688@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Family Fun,Holidays,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:DATES: Opens Saturday\, November 28\, 2026 and runs through Th
 ursday\, December 31\, 2026\nHOURS: Mon-Sat 12-6 p.m.\, Sun 12-4 p.m.\; De
 c 24 and Dec 31 12-4 p.m.\; closed Dec 25 and Sun. Dec 27\nLOCATION: Maric
 h Music\, 62 E. Market St.\, Corning\, NY 14830 (2nd-floor gallery\, stair
 s only)\nCOST: Suggested $2 cash donation to benefit the Food Bank of the 
 Southern Tier\nDESCRIPTION:\nThe World's Largest Traveling Harmonica Museu
 m is at Marich Music for the holidays! Ken VanEtten\, retired Corning scho
 ol music teacher\, fills the upstairs gallery with more than 1\,500 harmon
 icas in over 50 displays: the World's Largest Harmonica (donated by the Fa
 bulous Sgro Brothers)\, the world's loudest harmonica\, harmonicas shaped 
 like cars\, blimps\, airplanes\, vegetables and animals\, harmonicas with 
 trumpets\, horns and bells\, the rare Elmira harmonica (National Harmonica
  Company\, 1919 to the early 1920s)\, and the 20th century told through ha
 rmonica boxes\, from early flight and two world wars to the golden age of 
 radio. Admission is a suggested $2 cash donation to the Food Bank of the S
 outhern Tier. The gallery is on the second floor and is accessible by stai
 rs only.\nClick here for full details\nClick here to learn more about Mari
 ch Music\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/
 78515463/20261128120000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515463/20261128120000
END:VEVENT
