BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prohibition Walking Tour: Repeal Day Edition
DTSTART:20261205T220000Z
DTEND:20261205T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:0bdaa897440f22fb8d451e3a4cca94bf7caae68a@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:Event by The History Center in Tompkins County\n110 North Tiog
 a Street within the Tompkins Center for History & Culture\, Ithaca\, NY\nD
 uration: 1 hr\nPublic\nOn December 5\, 1933\, Prohibition came to an end\,
  and Ithaca could finally pour a legal drink again. We’re marking the an
 niversary with a special Repeal Day run of our Prohibition History Walking
  Tour. Start at The History Center and walk downtown through the city’s 
 dry years: the speakeasies\, the raids\, the temperance crusaders and the 
 people who ignored them. The tour ends at The Strand Cafe\, our tour spons
 or\, where you’re welcome to stay and raise a glass to repeal. Tickets a
 re $15.\nWhat: 75 minute walking tour over sidewalks\, gravel paths\, and 
 grass - with a slight incline\nWhere: The History Center in Tompkins Count
 y\, 110 N Tioga St\, Ithaca NY 14850\nWho: This tour is designed for ages 
 16-116\nWear Comfortable Shoes\, Bring an Umbrella\, Jacket\, and Water Bo
 ttle\nWeather - this tour takes place rain or shine! In case of severe wea
 ther\, we’ll determine cancellations by 10:30 am the morning-of.\n\nSour
 ce: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515550/2026120
 5170000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515550/20261205170000
END:VEVENT
