BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Songs of the Shakers & Shape Note/Sacred Harp Singing
DTSTART:20261206T190000Z
DTEND:20261207T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261113T170946Z
UID:e5c216d606c05ebb10f0ad050129326a25cfde7d@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, December 6\, 2026\, at 2 pm\nA celebration of America
 ’s 250th birthday year with\nTwo Early American Singing Styles:\nSongs o
 f the Shakers &\nShape Note/Sacred Harp Singing\nConcert at 144 Cedar Stre
 et\, Corning\nWe celebrate America’s 250th birthday year with presentati
 ons of two early American singing styles. The presenters will explore Song
 s of the Shakers and Shape Note (or Sacred Harp) Singing.\nGuitarist\, com
 poser Liam Lawson will present his arrangements of Shaker songs he researc
 hed. A northeast musician\, Lawson is a music educator and a bit of an his
 torian and is a multi-instrumentalist.\nGlenn Eric Bean has been active in
  organizing and leading Sacred harp singing conventions\, contributing sig
 nificantly to the preservation and promotion of the living tradition of Sh
 ape Note Singing\, particularly in Ithaca. A group of singers will be with
  him to sing for us. The audience will have an opportunity to try a shape 
 note song\, at the end.\nThis special concert is free—donations optional
 . This concert is supported by a generous donation from Corning Incorporat
 ed as one of many 2026 gifts to the community in celebration of their 175 
 year anniversary. Congratulations and thank you to Corning\, Inc!\nA recep
 tion will follow instead of the usual intermission. bring snacks to share 
 if you want\, warm beverages will be provided.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - ht
 tps://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515566/20261206140000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78515566/20261206140000
END:VEVENT
