 d Hall\, Ithaca College.\nProgram: This joyful concert will feature an exc
 iting program with something for everyone\, including the Chaminade Concer
 tino (Op. 107) for Flute Solo with Band Accompaniment\, featuring flute so
 loist Liz Shuhan\, faculty member at the Opus Ithaca School of Music. Othe
 r works will include Festive Overture (Shostakovich)\, The Eighth Candle (
 Reisteter)\, Gloriam (Standridge)\, Snow on Snow (Vinther)\, Carol of the 
 Bells (Leontovich-Wilhousky\, arr. O'Loughlin)\, Winterscape (Lendt)\, Ges
 u Bambino (Yon-Martens\, arr. Reisteter\, featuring vocalist Mark Lawrence
 )\, and some children's holiday tunes.\nBring your friends and family to t
 his wonderful event to celebrate a beautiful time of year. Admission is al
 ways free\, donations are always welcome. Refreshments will be offered fol
 lowing the performance.\nQuestions? Feel free to reach out via Facebook me
